msgid "``record_only`` dry run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:447
msgid "``None`` — nothing was executed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:449
msgid ""
"``diagnostics`` are read from the solver's ``.sta`` and ``.msg`` files. "
"Its attributes are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:457
msgid "``sta_verdict``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:458
msgid ""
"``COMPLETED`` | ``NOT_COMPLETED`` | ``ABORTED`` | ``INDETERMINATE`` (the "
"last means no ``.sta`` verdict line was found)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:460
msgid "``errors``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:461
msgid "Deduplicated, truncated ERROR lines — usually the fastest read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:462
msgid "``error_total`` / ``warning_total``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:463
msgid "Counts before dedup/truncation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:464
msgid "``increments``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:465
msgid ""
"Completed increments (best-effort). A low count with ``NOT_COMPLETED`` "
"points at early divergence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:467
msgid "``source_files``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:468
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{kind: absolute path}`` for each file actually read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:469
msgid "``solver_type``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:470
msgid "``standard`` | ``explicit`` | ``unknown``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:475
msgid "``phases`` entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:477
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each entry is ``{phase, status, started_at, ended_at, duration_s, "
"error}``. ``phase`` is one of ``compile``, ``preparation``, "
"``preflight``, ``pre_extraction``, ``simulation``, ``post_extraction``. "
"Only phases that ran appear, so the last entry is where a failed job "
"stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:483
msgid "Reading results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:485
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A large result is written beside the job as a CSV and referenced by a "
"sidecar envelope (``{\"__file__\": ..., \"format\": ..., \"shape\": "
"...}``) rather than inlined. These helpers accept both inline values and "
"envelopes, so you do not need to care which you got:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:490
msgid ""
":func:`~ABQflow.load_field` -- one field of one outcome as "
"``numpy.ndarray``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:491
msgid ":func:`~ABQflow.iter_fields` -- ``(job_name, ndarray)`` across a batch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:492
msgid ""
":func:`~ABQflow.degenerate_from_array` -- 2D ``numpy.ndarray`` from "
"scalar results across a batch. Non-``COMPLETED`` jobs become "
"``default_value`` (``nan``) rows with a warning, so array rows stay "
"aligned with jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/basic_batch.rst:495
msgid ""
"``load_field`` and ``iter_fields`` need ``output_dir`` to find a sidecar "
"file; they warn and return ``None`` if it is missing or the file has been"
" moved."
msgstr ""

